==Trivia==
*Both stages' Japanese names contain puns:
**[[Heaven and Hell (Merciless)|Heaven and Hell]]'s Japanese name, Gokuraku Edo (獄楽穢土), makes a pun on the word ''gokuraku'' (極楽, meaning paradise, or the [[wikipedia:Pure Land|Pure Land]] in Buddhism). Normally it would be spelled 極楽, but here it's 獄楽 - the first kanji is replaced by one meaning "prison". The word ''edo'' (穢土) refers to the opposite of the Pure Land, the land of the living or "Impure Land".
**This pun is also used in [[The Pure Land (Merciless)|The Pure Land]]'s Japanese name, which is nearly identical except that it has ''jōdo'' (浄土, pure land) instead of ''edo''.
**[[Okame's Teahouse (Merciless)|Okame's Teahouse]]'s Japanese name, Meido Kissa OKAME (冥土喫茶OKAME), has a pun on ''meido kissa'', which would normally mean "maid café", but the stage's name spells ''meido'' as 冥土, meaning the underworld; the world of the dead. Like the Pure Land, 冥土 is a Buddhist term.

